From 0541a7e504010d0b45fa659f27dcf55de8d4b319 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: havok2-htwo <havok2-htwo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 15:11:39 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 04/17] port 9e64a578: serve: STRATA_SLOT_PARK=1 parks a
 pipelined slot's conversation, reply included

Placed beside upstream's park_slot (#2526, a synchronous park before an
overwrite, which returns early with --mtp and no --batch-mtp):
- No double park: park_slot first calls slot_park_instead(b); when slot
  b's capture is pending, that image goes to the cache (slot_park_put)
  and park_slot returns.  So every upstream overwrite site that calls
  park_slot (the BADM admission, a BYIELD give_way, a co-read) waits for
  the capture and parks it.  The BADM admission calls slot_park_put
  itself first, as in the source, so a failed copy there still ends the
  engine; at the other sites a failure is logged and the slot is
  overwritten, as park_slot's own failures are.  With no capture pending
  park_slot runs unchanged (after a put it finds the image: holds()).
- supersedes_richer (#4420): with STRATA_SUPERSEDE_PREFIX it now asks
  the prefix rule (the entries drop_superseded would drop under it), and
  a checkpoint marked slot_turn does not count as richer (the next slot
  image leaves it behind on purpose).  slot_park_put itself does not
  refuse on it: its image carries the chain the prompt was read with,
  the system prompt's root included, which is what #4420 protects.
- drop_superseded_by_prefix keeps the guarded borrow donor and uses
  upstream's erase() (serials), via superseded_by_prefix(), shared with
  supersedes_richer.
- Off with STRATA_PIPED_MTP (pmtp): its commits are deferred past a
  slot's last window, so the slot is not final at BDONE.  The hooks are
  in the non-pmtp pipelined pump only: BDONE (capture start), the #879
  nonfinite exit, the group pick (a pad row over a slot still being
  captured waits; a drain or a due STRATA_PIPE_ADAPT_EVERY round ends
  the wait) and the group start (VERIFY before a pad row).  The wait
  line is printed with the pipelined all-idle line (no idle_report
  lambda upstream).  No PIPE_OVERLAP (ov_S) in v0.2.12.
- The SLOT_PARK state and lambdas sit after the slot groups (pg); the
  main-session hunks use F17's renamed capture (park_capture_*,
  park_capture_on).  slot_chain_start / slot_chain_settle join
  STRATA_CKPT_ASYNC before copying `checks`.
- The park decision: the slot that parks the conversation is checked
  before upstream's borrow branch, so the main sessions' copy is never
  parked beside the slot's image.  draftless is honoured at the four
  incoming validate/restore sites and SNAPSHOT_VERIFY.
- BSlot{} resets (upstream's admissions) clear parks/chain with the rest.

Not ported: conversation_copy.hpp's copy_checkpoint_beating does not
copy slot_turn (as in production); parked_prefix_tokens (park gain)
still asks the chain rule.

(cherry picked from commit 9e64a5782655b35c760593771689316c9bc622da)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
